    "quote": "Suppose we use a stochastically smoothed GBPA with perturbation $\\eta Z$, with $Z$'s generalized hazard rate being bounded: $h_\\alpha(x) \\le C, \\forall x \\in \\RR$ for some $\\alpha \\in [0,1)$, and $\\EE[\\max Z_i] - \\EE[Z_1] \\le Q(N)$ ... Then, if we set $\\eta = (\\frac{2CNT}{(1-\\alpha) Q(N)})^{1/(2-\\alpha)}$, the expected regret of GBPA is no greater than $2 \\times (\\frac{2C}{1-\\alpha})^{1/(2-\\alpha)} \\times (NT)^{1/(2-\\alpha)} \\times Q(N)^{(1-\\alpha)/(2-\\alpha)}$."
